# ---- ML / data artifacts (biomedical RAG) ----
# Datasets & corpora (PubMed, PubMedQA, BioASQ, etc.) — track via download scripts, not git.
# data/* rather than data/ — git will not descend into an excluded directory, so the negations
# below only work if the exclusion is on the contents (the same reason docs/* is written that way).
data/*
# Tracked exceptions: the small identity artifacts whose hashes go into every run manifest. These
# are membership lists, not data — splits.json is the frozen dev/test split (§3 requires it checked
# in), and gold_pmids.json is the dedup key set (ADR-0012 §1).
!data/splits.json
!data/gold_pmids.json
datasets/
corpus/
# Tracked exception: the corpus manifest — seed, the guards' counts, the fingerprint, and the 2M
# PMID list. ADR-0012 §1 requires the ID list committed, and `CorpusDraw.fingerprint` hashes the
# list rather than the parameters, so the list is the only thing the hash can be checked against.
# `corpus.jsonl` (~2 GB of abstracts) and `prescan.jsonl` stay out — they are reproducible from it.
# Three lines because git will not descend into an excluded directory.
!data/corpus/
data/corpus/*
!data/corpus/corpus_manifest.json
*.jsonl
*.parquet
*.arrow
*.csv
*.tsv

# …but the per-question records under docs/harvest/ are results, not data. `!docs/harvest/`
# higher up only rescues them from the `docs/*` rule; `*.jsonl` above still wins, so the
# least-processed-value artifacts that back every number in the paper were silently dropped.
!docs/harvest/**/*.jsonl

# Retrieval indexes & embeddings (BM25 / dense / FAISS)
indexes/
index/
*.faiss
*.index
*.bin
embeddings/
*.npy
*.npz
*.pkl
*.pickle

